{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/number"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/number","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Distinguishes between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number).","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"number","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV6numberAA14MXLNumberLevelVSgvp"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"number"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNumberLevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate/number":{"title":"number","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/number","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/number","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Distinguishes between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number)."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLArpeggiate","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}